{"skill":{"slug":"spreadsheet","displayName":"Spreadsheet"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1771372027219,"changelog":"Initial release","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3051,"sha256":"0d73287d8267eb7bb54d193004ab9b963a43e6794b1fbf666091af7bf3d480dc","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"csv.md","size":1161,"sha256":"acab0dc41f053c26cb55eed20f1aed2d1f5c8131bdbec8088295834e20e02433","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"excel.md","size":1144,"sha256":"20c912156a8e723e7395e39c1330b594274c6cc6f9b9c386e318c88263afeb0f","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"google-sheets.md","size":1358,"sha256":"8b4d18ef084ec58b4871bd952a829174c4fcc526007e41f13c8e70111ee18de4","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"memory-template.md","size":862,"sha256":"59247efd6880e56e28e55fd750cd0960829060f72fec38dd1d975fb904be0f0d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2348,"sha256":"688a12071655ff89bad2734a187e7d52bd0fc4885932a3e833b78c97534b9b2d","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789071710504,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"fd09437c7bc29879408b66f353df9eaca39363c0d7d29a65ed9a850476f3ee7b","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/fd09437c7bc29879408b66f353df9eaca39363c0d7d29a65ed9a850476f3ee7b","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: spreadsheet\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill is classified as suspicious due to its direct handling of sensitive API credentials (`credentials.json`) for Google Sheets authentication, as explicitly instructed in `google-sheets.md` and referenced in `memory-template.md`. While necessary for the skill's functionality, this introduces a high-risk operation. Although `SKILL.md` states the skill 'NEVER stores passwords, API keys', it instructs the agent to load and use a file containing them, creating a potential vulnerability if the agent is compromised or if file paths are manipulated (e.g., via path traversal). The skill also performs extensive file I/O operations on user-provided paths, which, without robust input sanitization, could lead to arbitrary file read/write vulnerabilities.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779164972084},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":76,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":8,"checkedAt":1789071710504},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a coherent spreadsheet helper skill, with expected but sensitive Google Sheets credential and write examples that users should scope carefully.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Creating ~/spreadsheet for schemas, preferences, exports, and project metadata is proportionate, but users should treat saved spreadsheet IDs, URLs, and credential references as sensitive.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The package is Markdown-only, declares no required binaries, and includes no executable scripts, install hooks, remote payload retrieval, or dependency installation.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The main instructions limit activity to user-requested spreadsheets and user paths, but the Google Sheets examples include write and append calls without a nearby mutation warning.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill persists schema memory under ~/spreadsheet and explicitly says it does not self-modify; the memory template’s service_account path should be handled as a sensitive reference rather than a stored secret.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill purpose is spreadsheet reading, writing, analysis, and schema memory across Google Sheets, Excel, and CSV; the documented capabilities match that purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Before installing, ensure any Google service account has access only to intended spreadsheets, confirm write and append ranges before use, and avoid storing actual secrets in ~/spreadsheet memory files.","findings":"[AR2] expected: The matched phrase is in a trap warning that says to confirm before loading many rows; it does not suppress refusals or safety warnings.\n[PE3] expected: The Google Sheets authentication example uses a local credentials.json service-account file, which is expected for this integration but should be user-provided and least-privileged.\n[PE3] expected: The memory template stores a service-account file path, not the credential contents; this is integration-relevant but should be scoped and not used to expose secrets.\n[SQP-2] expected: Remote update and append examples are expected for a spreadsheet write skill, though users should confirm the spreadsheet ID and range because these calls mutate Google Sheets data.\n[SQP-2] expected: The credential-path template is relevant to Google Sheets setup, but the skill would be safer if it warned not to store credential material in memory.\n[SDI-4] expected: Formula-preservation guidance is purpose-aligned, but the data_only=True wording overstates the direct risk because reading cached values does not by itself destroy formulas.\n[SQP-3] expected: A number-locale preference is expected for spreadsheet formatting; en-US appears to be a template default and should be user-adjusted.\n[SDI-2] expected: Google Sheets URLs and service-account configuration fit the declared multi-platform spreadsheet scope, with the same credential-handling caution noted above.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789071710504}}}}}